title: Government Formation
new-page: true

= Forming a Government

[? if year = 1931 : The Constituent Cortes elected in June has returned a large left-republican and Socialist majority. The Republican-Socialist coalition that has governed since April - the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>, the Republican Left, and the Radical Socialists - now has a real electoral mandate behind it. ?][? if year = 1933 : The Cortes elected in November has returned a majority for the <span style="color: #d9a441;">Radical Party</span> and the <span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span>. The Republican-Socialist coalition has lost its majority; the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> must decide how to respond. ?][? if year = 1936 : The Popular Front - <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>, <span style="color: #8a0303;">**PCE**</span>, the Republican Left, and the regionalist parties - has won a majority in the Cortes. The old argument between the Prietista and Caballerista wings of the party resurfaces: does the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> take cabinet seats, or support the government from outside? ?]

- @rs_1931_confirm: Confirm the Republican-Socialist coalition; Azaña becomes President of the Council of Ministers.
- @rs_1931_gradual: Confirm the coalition, but urge Azaña to pace the reform program more cautiously.
- @radical_ceda_accept: Accept opposition; let the Radical Party and the CEDA govern.
- @radical_ceda_defy: Attempt to hold together a left coalition despite lacking a majority.
- @pf_join: Join the Popular Front government - the Prietista position.
- @pf_tolerate: Support the Popular Front from outside the cabinet, without taking ministries - the Caballerista position.

@rs_1931_confirm
choose-if: year = 1931
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist = 1; in_radical_ceda = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 1; psoe_toleration = 0; izq_rep_in_government = 1; radical_in_government = 1; ceda_in_government = 0; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Azaña"; chancellor_party = "IR"; interior_minister = "Casares Quiroga"; interior_minister_party = "IR"; reformist_dissent -= 2

Manuel Azaña, the Republican Left's leader and the coalition's dominant figure, becomes President of the Council of Ministers, with our full backing. The government presses ahead with land reform, military reform, and the secularizing articles of the new Constitution.

@rs_1931_gradual
choose-if: year = 1931
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist = 1; in_radical_ceda = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 1; psoe_toleration = 0; izq_rep_in_government = 1; radical_in_government = 1; ceda_in_government = 0; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Azaña"; chancellor_party = "IR"; interior_minister = "Casares Quiroga"; interior_minister_party = "IR"; church_relation += 2; left_dissent += 2

Azaña becomes President of the Council of Ministers, but at our urging the coalition paces its reforms more carefully, hoping to avoid handing the CEDA and the Church more grievances than necessary. The Caballerista left grumbles at the caution.

@radical_ceda_accept
choose-if: year = 1933
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist = 0; in_radical_ceda = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 0; psoe_toleration = 0; izq_rep_in_government = 0; radical_in_government = 1; ceda_in_government = 1; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Lerroux"; chancellor_party = "Radical"; interior_minister = "Rico Avello"; interior_minister_party = "Radical"; justice_minister_party = "Radical"; finance_minister_party = "Radical"; agriculture_minister_party = "Radical"; labor_minister_party = "Radical"; left_dissent += 5; ceda_relation += 5; radical_relation += 3

Alejandro Lerroux forms a government of the <span style="color: #d9a441;">Radical Party</span>, tolerated in the Cortes by the <span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span>. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> goes into opposition for the first time since the Republic's founding - the start of the *bienio negro*, the "black two years." Land reform stalls; several of our own reforms are rolled back.

@radical_ceda_defy
choose-if: year = 1933
on-arrival: republican_socialist_failed = 1; in_republican_socialist = 0; in_radical_ceda = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 0; psoe_toleration = 0; izq_rep_in_government = 0; radical_in_government = 1; ceda_in_government = 1; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Lerroux"; chancellor_party = "Radical"; interior_minister = "Rico Avello"; interior_minister_party = "Radical"; justice_minister_party = "Radical"; finance_minister_party = "Radical"; agriculture_minister_party = "Radical"; labor_minister_party = "Radical"; left_dissent += 8; radical_relation -= 5; coup_progress += 1

We try to hold the old coalition together despite the new Cortes arithmetic, hoping to deny the Radicals and the CEDA a government. It is a doomed effort: without a majority, the attempt collapses within weeks, and Alejandro Lerroux forms a Radical-CEDA government regardless - only now, having tried and failed to cling to power, we enter opposition looking weaker, not stronger. The <span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span> and authoritarian right take fresh confidence from the spectacle of a government that could not survive its own election.

@pf_join
choose-if: year = 1936
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist = 0; in_radical_ceda = 0; in_popular_front = 1; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 1; psoe_toleration = 0; izq_rep_in_government = 1; radical_in_government = 0; ceda_in_government = 0; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Azaña"; chancellor_party = "IR"; interior_minister = "Amós Salvador"; interior_minister_party = "IR"; foreign_minister_party = "IR"; agriculture_minister = "Ruiz-Funes"; agriculture_minister_party = "IR"; left_dissent += 3; ceda_relation -= 3

The Prietista wing of the party carries the argument: we take cabinet seats in Azaña's Popular Front government, alongside the Republican Left. It is the clearest statement yet that reform and revolution both run through this government - but it commits the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>'s fortunes to a government the right is already calling illegitimate.

@pf_tolerate
choose-if: year = 1936
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist = 0; in_radical_ceda = 0; in_popular_front = 1; in_workers_alliance = 0; psoe_in_government = 0; psoe_toleration = 1; izq_rep_in_government = 1; radical_in_government = 0; ceda_in_government = 0; monarchist_in_government = 0; pce_in_government = 0; falange_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Azaña"; chancellor_party = "IR"; interior_minister = "Amós Salvador"; interior_minister_party = "IR"; foreign_minister_party = "IR"; justice_minister_party = "IR"; labor_minister_party = "IR"; finance_minister_party = "IR"; agriculture_minister = "Ruiz-Funes"; agriculture_minister_party = "IR"; left_strength += 3

The Caballerista wing prevails: the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> will support the Popular Front government's program in the Cortes, but will not take ministries - preserving its independence, and its ability to claim it was never responsible for the government's compromises. Azaña's cabinet is drawn entirely from the Republican Left and its allies.
